Subject: [PATCH 18/29] docs: what the driver package is, corrected - and
 build.sh checks the binary's digest

The correction the previous commit's message promised but did not contain: docs/gpu-safety.md never
got the driver section (it was lost when the workspace was restored from an older snapshot), and
docs/progress-log.md still said the answer was "a newer PanVK-kbase". It is not, because there is
nothing newer - and the proof is now in the docs rather than in my reasoning: the installed
libpanvk_backend.so hashes to 0b8eaf709cd3...60c820, which is the digest upstream's rc2 notes publish
for libvulkan_panfrost-glibc-aarch64.so. Same file, not same size.

Both docs now also retract two claims I made about upstream's release notes after reading them
properly. They do not describe a present-after-two-frames hang - that is our measurement, ours alone.
And they say nothing about this guest's display server; the X11 dependence in the .so is about how
the binary was built, not a statement about supported WSI. What the notes DO say matters more: the
rc2 binary has never been run on a device at all, and upstream is asking for PanProbe reports, which
is a bounded experiment on this phone that involves neither Steam nor the chroot.

build.sh gained EXPECTED_BACKEND_SHA256, comparing the extracted .so against the published digest
instead of only the download's, so a repackage proves it carries the official build; the packaging
workflow passes it through as an optional input with rc2's value in a comment. The doc no longer says
"248 lines", which I can no longer verify from the original zip.

